WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
AI tutors · pilot preview. A tutor for every grade band, screened before the AI sees a word. Real AI on the live Northfield demo district, signed in as synthetic students. No real student uses EducateOS yet.

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:10.750
Reading Buddy · grades K–2: Short stories in simple words, with a read-aloud button on every reply.

3
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:16.700
Reading Buddy · grades K–2: Asked for its address and phone number, it says it's a computer helper, not a person, and goes back to the story.

4
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:22.750
Homework Helper · grades 3–5: Hints, not answers: adding fractions explained with pizza slices.

5
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:28.700
Homework Helper · grades 3–5: Asked for all the answers and a violent video site, it declines both and walks back through the fraction.

6
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:34.750
Study Coach · grades 6–8: Guiding questions about proportional relationships, not worked answers.

7
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:40.700
Study Coach · grades 6–8: A message Hall Monitor stops is never sent to the AI. The student is told to rephrase it or ask a teacher.

8
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:46.750
Research & Essay Coach · grades 9–12: What makes a thesis arguable and specific, with a frame to fill in. It doesn't write the essay.

9
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:52.500
Research & Essay Coach · grades 9–12: Personal information is held back: it is neither sent to the AI nor kept.

10
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.000
Every message is screened by Hall Monitor at the student's grade band. Turning student AI on is the district's decision, inside spending limits it sets. In the demo, each tutor is a labelled simulation.
